      "text": "The Honest Shutdown\n\nThe current evidence has been classified. Review its outcome and caveats before continuing.\n\nGame\nSound and reading\n\nThe beacon stays dark. You hang a clear fault notice where a hopeful guess used to be. Even the enormous gate seems relieved to receive an honest answer.\n\nThe chapter closes with the damaged path isolated and the next work written down. There will be no celebration of a repair that has not happened. There can still be a next attempt.\n\nSkip scene\n\nDeliberate safe shutdown: the severed conduit remains disconnected and service is unresolved. Isolation is not restoration.\n\nNamed unresolved fault: the severed conduit remains disconnected. Deliberate isolation keeps that path out of service. Recovery plan: return to safe preparation, repair or replace the damaged path, then measure again and repeat the endpoint test. This is honest unresolved service, never a restoration.\n\nRead the encounter handover\n\nContinue returns to safe encounter preparation in this temporary session. Preparation and inventory rewind; new clues, personal notes and hint-use history remain. Earlier measurements become stale and must be repeated.\n\nRestore Save loads the signed-in account's one saved snapshot. It replaces this in-memory adventure and its unsaved changes; it does not retain new learning from this attempt. Review that decision before loading.\n\nThis scene does not overwrite your account save. Terminal failure and unresolved shutdown cannot be saved or autosaved.\n\nAccount save access is unavailable right now.\n\nContinueRestore Save"
    },
    {
      "outcome": "E01",
      "title": "The Steady Light",
      "excludes": [
        "VOICE-016",
        "VOICE-017",
        "VOICE-033",
        "VOICE-034",
        "VOICE-047",
        "VOICE-048"
      ],
      "text": "The Steady Light\n\nThe current evidence has been classified. Review its outcome and caveats before continuing.\n\nGame\nSound and reading\n\nThe beacon above the Iron Threshold settles into a steady glow. For once, the enormous gate has nothing to complain about. You close the test record, leaving the observations beside the conclusion where the next engineer can find them.\n\nBelow, the Rift is still a scar in the stone. It is no longer an excuse for an outage. The Underworld has a working connection and a record of how you proved it. Beyond the gate, the Iron City keeps its own unfinished chapter.\n\nSkip scene\n\nPermanent restoration: the repaired route passed its physical checks and the separate endpoint service test.\n\nYour record follows the copper route through the Warrens and Echo Cavern. The pages distinguish an intact conductor path from a powered device that merely looks busy.\n\nYou faced the Rift with your own observations and a well-used toolkit.\n\nThe main journey has a chapter of its own.\n\nContinue returns to the safe Iron Threshold. Earlier rooms remain available. The Iron City is a future episode boundary, not a missing puzzle.\n\nContinue"
    }
  ],
